 EVALUATION PROCEDURE                                             9634 1451   23
                                                                  9634 1451   24
 Adopted procedure is based on careful theoretical                9634 1451   25
 analysis utilizing available experimental data and               9634 1451   26
 nuclear reaction model calculations.                             9634 1451   27
                                                                  9634 1451   28
 Available experimental data were interpreted  using              9634 1451   29
 nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-3 by M. Herman                9634 1451   30
 et al [EMP]. This code integrates into a single                  9634 1451   31
 system a number of important modules and features:               9634 1451   32
                                                                  9634 1451   33
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 9634 1451   34
   coupled-channels (ECIS06 by J. Raynal)                         9634 1451   35
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    9634 1451   36
   HRTW width fluctuation correction                              9634 1451   37
 - Quantum-mechanical MSD TUL model (codes ORION &                9634 1451   38
   TRISTAN by H. Lenske), and MSC NVWY model                      9634 1451   39
 - Exciton model with angular momentum coupling                   9634 1451   40
   (code DEGAS by E. Betak and P. Oblozinsky) that                9634 1451   41
   represents a good approximation to the DSD model               9634 1451   42
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      9634 1451   43
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 9634 1451   44
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                9634 1451   45
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   9634 1451   46
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                9634 1451   47
   discrete transitions                                           9634 1451   48
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL library [RIPL]                9634 1451   49
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                9634 1451   50
   level density, discrete levels, fission barriers               9634 1451   51
   and gamma strength functions based on the RIPL                 9634 1451   52
   library [RIPL]                                                 9634 1451   53
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              9634 1451   54
   EXFOR/CSISRS library                                           9634 1451   55
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A. Trkov)                    9634 1451   56
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 9634 1451   57
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                9634 1451   58
   PrePro codes by R. Cullen                                      9634 1451   59
 - Checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                        9634 1451   60
 - Support for NJOY                                               9634 1451   61
                                                                  9634 1451   62
 PARAMETERIZATIONS                                                9634 1451   63
                                                                  9634 1451   64
 Following models and parameters were used in the                 9634 1451   65
 current evaluation:                                              9634 1451   66
                                                                  9634 1451   67
 Discrete levels were taken from the RIPL-3 level                 9634 1451   68
 file, based on the 2007 version of ENSDF.                        9634 1451   69
 EMPIRE-specific level densities                                  9634 1451   70
 ENDF formatting enabled                                          9634 1451   71
 Exclusive spectra available up to emission loop #  5             9634 1451   72
 Coupled Channels (ECIS) used for direct inelastic scattering     9634 1451   73
 Emission width of ejectile 0 from 244Cm multiplied by   3.265    9634 1451   74
 Exciton model calculations with code PCROSS                      9634 1451   75
 Cluster emission in terms of the Iwamoto-Harada model            9634 1451   76
 Kalbach systematics angular distributions (see RIPL-1)           9634 1451   77
 Mean free path parameter in PCROSS set to  1.4 (Recommended ~ 1.59634 1451   78
 Exciton model calculations with code DEGAS                       9634 1451   79
 For all nuclei: advanced treatment of fission                    9634 1451   80
 FISBAR  in all nuclei set to  0.000                              9634 1451   81
 FISDEN  in all nuclei set to  1.000                              9634 1451   82
 FISOPT  in all nuclei set to  1.000                              9634 1451   83
 E1 strength function set to MLO3                                 9634 1451   84
 GDR parameters from RIPL-2/Exp.data+Plujko systematics           9634 1451   85
